{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 38, :comments ["<b>to give you the land.</b> As we say at the end of tractate Ketuvot: A person should always dwell in the land of Israel, even in a city whose majority is idolaters, and not dwell outside the land, even in a city whose majority is Israel — for whoever dwells outside the land is like one who has no god, as it is said: להיות לכם לאלהים. And likewise David says: כי גרשוני היום וגו'."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:38.203035100Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}